course: dictionary
lesson: 1620
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word cherry can name a fruit, a tree, a colour, or the wood from the tree.
explain: Look at the clues. «One clip shows one moment, not the whole person; choosing only the bits that fit is called cherry-picking.» Cherry-picking has nothing to do with fruit. The clue is «choosing only the bits that fit», so it means choosing only the best parts.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «A cherry on top» means a nice extra, like the fruit on top of a cake. Does «a nice extra» still make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A cherry is a small round fruit with a hard stone in the middle.
fact: A cherry tree has pink or white blossom in spring.
fact: Cherry is also a bright red colour, as in cherry-red.
fact: «A swallowed cherry stone usually just passes through the body.» The stone is the seed, and it does not grow inside you.
fact: «Cherry-picking» means choosing only the best bits.
exercise: «One clip shows one moment; choosing only the bits that fit is called cherry-picking.» What does cherry-picking mean? | Growing a cherry tree | Painting something bright red | Eating cherries in a pie | *Choosing only the best bits
exercise: «Her cardigan was cherry-red.» What colour is cherry-red? | Dark green | Pink and white | *Bright red | Yellow
exercise: «A swallowed cherry stone usually just passes through the body.» What is the stone of a cherry? | A long thin stalk | A pink flower on the tree | A reddish piece of wood | *A hard stone in the middle of the fruit
test: «She added a cherry on top of her cake.» What does a cherry on top mean? | A small red fruit | *A nice extra | A tree in the garden | A piece of wood
test: «The table was made from cherry, so it glowed with a reddish shine.» What is cherry here? | A spring blossom | A small fruit with a stone | *The reddish wood of the cherry tree | A bright red colour
exam: «He cherry-picked the best ideas for his project.» What does cherry-picked mean? | Grew fruit on a tree | Threw every idea away | *Chose only the best ones | Painted them bright red
